---
// Story 1-6. Handstand coaching — KEPT but MINIMAL and DEMOTED (A1).
//
// ⚠️ MOVED FROM /handstand-coaching/ AT THE ROOT. This is a nesting
// normalisation, not a rename for its own sake: every other service lives under
// /services/, and one at the root is the odd one out. The old URL 301s here
// (story 1-7, D4).
//
// The old page's meta description carried "chiriopractor". That typo is fixed
// here and is a correction, not a copy rewrite.
//
// ⚠️ THIS PAGE HAD THE CLASS TIME WRONG. It said "Sunday 11am" while
// /services/group-classes/ said "Saturday 10am", both live at once. Keegan
// confirmed SATURDAY (SM-9, 2026-07-31). The time is always paired with the
// booking check because he cancels the class often — see group-classes.astro for
// the full reasoning.
//
// AUTHORITY LIVES ON /about/, NOT HERE (Manny A1). The acrobatics-and-
// handbalancing background is the credential behind the movement work and it is
// told as a story on the About page. This page is the service: what it is, what
// it costs, how to get it.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookCta from '../../components/BookCta.astro';
import { service } from '../../lib/schema.mjs';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../lib/site-env.mjs';
import business from '../../data/business.json' with { type: 'json' };
import bridge from '../../assets/site/IMG_1667.jpg';
// LN-6 / 1-15 editorial pass. The handstand page led with a photograph of a
// BRIDGE. A previous pass noticed and wrote honest alt text for it, which was
// the right instinct applied to the wrong end of the problem — accurate alt on
// a mismatched lead still leaves a handstand page whose only picture is not a
// handstand. The bridge is genuinely useful further down, where the copy is
// about the shoulder and spine range the skill needs, so it moves rather than
// goes. Straight-line hold here; the straddle lives on /about/.
import handstand from '../../assets/site/IMG_1551.jpg';

const LAST_CHANGED = new Date('2026-07-31T00:00:00+10:00');

// No offers node — Cliniko has no billable item for the class (G-8).
const SERVICE_NODE = service(SITE_URL, 'handstand-class');
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Handstand Coaching, Northern Beaches | ${business.name}`}
  description="Handstand coaching and weekly beginner handstand classes on Sydney's Northern Beaches. From never going upside down to a confident 10-second hold."
  updated={LAST_CHANGED}
>
  <script slot="head-jsonld" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(SERVICE_NODE)} />

  <h1>Handstand coaching</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Structured handstand training for complete beginners through to people refining more advanced
    skills. Strength, balance, mobility and body awareness all develop through this one skill, which
    is why I keep coaching it alongside the clinical work.
  </p>

  <Image
    src={handstand}
    alt="Keegan holding a straight handstand in a mirrored studio, body stacked vertically over both hands with his legs together"
    widths={[384, 768]}
    sizes="(max-width: 44rem) 100vw, 24rem"
    class="page-img tall"
    loading="eager"
    fetchpriority="high"
  />

  <h2>Who is handstand training for?</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who wants to get upside down, at any starting point. Didn’t everyone want to do these as a
    child? Whether you’re chasing the thrill of finally holding it away from the wall, want a fun and
    challenging addition to your training, or simply love the idea of being upside down again,
    handstand coaching is a structured, supportive way to get there.
  </p>
  <p>
    I work with complete beginners through to those refining more advanced handstand skills, although
    if you’re an elite level gymnast or Cirque du Soleil performer, I probably can’t help.
  </p>

  <h2>What does a one-to-one session involve?</h2>
  <p>
    A completely personalised hour. I analyse what level you are up to and identify the things
    holding you back most, then we work through drills that address them with in-the-moment feedback.
    Whether you’re a complete beginner or have been working on handstands for a while, I can help.
  </p>
  {/* Described as what it IS — a bridge, not a handstand. Alt text that
      oversells the photo is a small lie to the one reader who cannot see it.
      It earns its place HERE, against copy about the drills and the range the
      skill demands, rather than as the lead on a page about handstands. */}
  <Image
    src={bridge}
    alt="Keegan in a bridge position, hands and feet on the floor and hips lifted, demonstrating shoulder and spine extension"
    widths={[384, 768]}
    sizes="(max-width: 44rem) 100vw, 24rem"
    class="page-img tall"
  />

  <p>
    <strong>Location and how to book.</strong> The location is up to you. I can meet you at your
    home, outside, in a neutral location, or I can organise a studio space hire. Because that means
    variable travel time and costs, this service is not on the online booking system. Email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> and we will organise a session that
    suits us both.
  </p>

  {/* LN-6 / 1-15 section rhythm. ONE band per page, and it always marks the
      same thing: the cheapest way in. Here that is the $20 class sitting under
      a page about one-to-one coaching, which is exactly the home page's band
      too. Consistent placement is what makes it read as a system rather than as
      decoration — see the note on `.band` in BaseLayout. */}
  <section class="band">
    <h2>Is there a class instead?</h2>
    <p class="class-time">
      <strong>Saturdays, 10&ndash;11am</strong> at Just Train Gym, Cromer, $20 for the hour. Numbers
      are small and I do sometimes cancel, so check the booking page for this week&rsquo;s session
      before you come.
    </p>
    <p>
      The class is designed for complete beginners and intermediate students, taking you from never
      going upside down to your first 10-second hold and beyond.
    </p>
    <p>
      We focus on proper technique and time-tested drills that build the strength and control to
      reliably stay upside down. The classes are community focused and designed to get you to a
      level where you can join the handstand meetups I organise around the Northern Beaches.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* ⚠️ THE BUTTON STAYS OUTSIDE THE BAND, DELIBERATELY. BookCta is an orange
      fill, and orange on sage is 2.11:1 — the one pairing the brand contract
      rules out outright. Inside a band it would also drag its hover (--ml-deep,
      which IS the ink the band would need) and its orange focus ring onto sage,
      so three separate values would each need re-deriving to keep one button in
      a coloured box. On paper every one of them is already verified, including
      the 19px/700 floor UD-21 turned on. A CTA immediately below its band reads
      as belonging to it regardless. */}
  <BookCta slug="handstand-class" label="Reserve a spot in the handstand class" />

  <h2>Where to next?</h2>
  <ul class="next-links">
    <li><a href="/services/group-classes/">All group classes</a> — including mobility and flexibility</li>
    <li><a href="/contact/">Book an appointment</a></li>
    <li><a href="/about/">About Keegan</a> — the acrobatics background behind this</li>
    <li><a href="/services/chiropractic-treatment/">Chiropractic &amp; Movement</a></li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
  /* SM-9. Time and caveat in one block — see group-classes.astro. */
  .class-time {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--ml-rule);
    padding-left: 0.9rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .next-links {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .next-links li {
    margin: 0.35rem 0;
  }
</style>
